# Core App Startup and Runtime Env Reference

> Updated: 2026-10-08
> Scope: actual `process.env` / `import.meta.env` usage in `apps/core-app/src`

## Startup and fallback status

### 1) Assistant startup state (current)

- `assistantModule` is always registered in the Core App startup module list; there is no environment-variable gate or Assistant-specific `shouldSkip` branch.
- The module creates no window at startup: the voice HUD is created by the first Fn/Ctrl voice command and hidden when each session ends. Since 2026-10-08 the floating ball and its `assistant.enabled` switch are gone, and loading the settings drops any leftover `assistant` and `floatingBall` fields.
- The Assistant has no separate switch any more; voice input is gated by `voiceInput.enabled` alone. The removed `TUFF_ENABLE_ASSISTANT_EXPERIMENT` flag is not a supported runtime variable, and startup no longer reports the old optional-module or environment-gate messages.

### 2) dev.source probe + local fallback (fixed)

- `DevPluginLoader` probes remote `manifest.json` first.
- If remote probe fails:
  - fall back to local `manifest.json` + local assets for current runtime only;
  - runtime overrides `dev.source=false` (not persisted);
  - records `DEV_SOURCE_FALLBACK_LOCAL` as warning.
- `REMOTE_MANIFEST_FAILED` remains fatal only when both remote and local fallback fail.

